        "content": "<p>This is the classical presentation theorem <code>SL₂(ℤ) ≅ ⟨s, t | s² = (st)³, s⁴ = 1⟩</code>. This requires Bass–Serre theory or the Ping-Pong lemma, neither of which is in Mathlib yet. Would this, or either of the routes to it, be useful to anyone?</p>",
        "id": 583602200,
        "sender_full_name": "Justin McClung",
        "timestamp": 1775325044
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I thought we had the ping pong lemma? Do I remember correctly that <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"282271\">@Bolton Bailey</span> or <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"470149\">@Joachim Breitner</span> proved it?</p>",
        "id": 583606983,
